---
import { tikkunTransition, tikkunImage, livingJourney, courseCta, site } from "../../data/content.js";
---

<section class="tikkun-transition">
  <p>{tikkunTransition}</p>
</section>

<section class="tikkun-image">
  <img src={tikkunImage} alt="Tikkun HaBris — Mevushat LaBrit" />
</section>

<section class="torah-narrative">
  <p>Our story begins with the first man and woman.</p>
  <p>Adam and Chava hid from one another in shame.</p>
  <p>With Avraham, something changed.</p>
  <p>Hashem commanded him to remove the ערלה—the barrier that stood between him and Sarah—so that their relationship could become a complete expression of love, holiness, and יחוד.</p>
  <p>Years later, when Avraham sent Eliezer to find a wife for Yitzchak, he told him:</p>
  <p class="hebrew-quote">"שים נא ידך תחת ירכי."</p>
  <p>In other words:</p>
  <p class="quote">"Take your oath while holding the place where I entered the Bris."</p>
  <p class="posed-question">Why wasn't Avraham embarrassed?</p>
  <p>Because he no longer experienced that place through the shame of Adam.</p>
  <p>He experienced it as the place through which he entered a Bris with Sarah and with Hashem—the place where יחוד became possible.</p>
  <p>The very place that Adam experienced as a source of shame became, for Avraham, the sign of his covenant with Sarah and with Hashem.</p>
  <p>This is the journey of Tikkun HaBris: not removing desire, but removing whatever prevents our deepest desires from becoming a source of love, יחוד, and holiness.</p>
</section>

<section class="living-journey">
  <h2>{livingJourney.heading}</h2>
  {livingJourney.paragraphs.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
</section>

<section class="course-cta">
  <div class="rule" style={`background:${site.accentColor}`}></div>
  <a href={site.signupUrl} class="cta-button" style={`background:${site.accentColor}`}>{courseCta.label}</a>
</section>

<style>
  .tikkun-transition {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: calc(var(--bhd-inner-space) * 0.6) 32px 0;
  }
  .tikkun-transition p {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 21px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: oklch(40% 0.012 75);
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .tikkun-image {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--bhd-hero-space) 40px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .tikkun-image img {
    width: 85%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .torah-narrative {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 32px 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .torah-narrative p {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    color: oklch(28% 0.012 75);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  .torah-narrative .hebrew-quote {
    font-size: 21px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: center;
    direction: rtl;
  }
  .torah-narrative .quote {
    font-size: 21px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .torah-narrative .posed-question {
    font-size: 23px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: center;
    color: oklch(22% 0.012 75);
  }
  .living-journey {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--bhd-section-space) 32px 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .living-journey h2 {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--bhd-section-space);
    color: oklch(22% 0.012 75);
  }
  .living-journey p {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    color: oklch(28% 0.012 75);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  .living-journey p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .course-cta {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--bhd-hero-space) 32px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .rule {
    width: 48px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--bhd-section-space);
  }
  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 18px 40px;
    color: white;
    font-family: "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
